1
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,340
Try lightening up on
peace and stepping away.

2
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
Kick a pebble and even your shoe flies off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
Onto the head of the
carpenter who was chopping away.

5
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed that we were still just kids.

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if you drop your energy somewhere.

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,640
Katsushika Kameari,
one yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,480
From the pointed hat, from the water bowl.

10
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:16,780
The sun sets toward Taishakuten Gate.

11
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow too, it will end just like this.

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:29,080
Katsushika Shibamata, happiness too.

13
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:34,020
Only once you were gone did I realize,
because I'm such a fool.

14
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,300
As family,

15
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:15,440
thank goodness the wedding
went off without a hitch.

16
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,080
Yes, this is Nakagawa.

17
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,440
Yes, it's Keiichi.

18
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:25,520
The Nakagawa Group
emergency general meeting.

19
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:35,960
Keiichi, what exactly is this
emergency general meeting today?

20
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,080
Well, I don't know either.

21
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:42,240
But my father was only supposed to return ten years from now,
and now he's coming back.

22
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,760
Something serious must have happened.

23
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:48,900
It's almost time.
Is President Ryuichiro really coming?

24
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:01,560
Tomo-san

25
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:08,980
You're right on time.

26
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:12,100
President, it's been a long time.

27
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,260
This is a waste of time.

28
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,300
I told you to skip the greetings.

29
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,580
Without further ado, the reason I've
gathered you all here today is none other than

30
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:20,220
the truth is

31
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:29,520
What is the meaning of a phone ringing during a meeting!
Turn it off within three seconds!

32
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,280
Good.

33
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,200
W-who is it? Someone who didn't
turn their phone off again?

34
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:43,440
It's me. It's my energy drink refill time.
Wait fifteen seconds.

35
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:12,140
Well, actually, yesterday the bidding for the
major joint Japan-U.S. project was held in New York,

36
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,776
and the Nakagawa Group,
which had never lost before,

37
00:04:15,826 --> 00:04:18,440
was defeated by its rival, the Ibishi Group.

38
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:22,660
What's more, the difference in the bid
amounts with Ibishi was only 1,000 dollars.

39
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:27,280
On a mega-business worth a total of one trillion dollars,
that's a gap of just 1,000 dollars!

40
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:29,380
Do you understand what this means?

41
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:33,000
N-no way, our bid amount was
leaked to the Ibishi Group!

42
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:34,680
Exactly.

43
00:04:34,730 --> 00:04:39,280
Only you gentlemen gathered here are
in a position to know the bid amount.

44
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:44,380
That means there's a traitor among us
who leaked our information to Ibishi.

45
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,420
It wasn't me.

46
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,580
Your department's in the red,
so you're the suspicious one.

47
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:51,920
You're one to talk.

48
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,820
Weren't you the one leaking
information from there?

49
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,580
L-let's all calm down, shall we?

50
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:58,980
Shut up!

51
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,200
Now that cracks have appeared in
the once-unified Nakagawa Group,

52
00:05:02,200 --> 00:05:05,020
I will find the traitor, no matter what.

53
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:08,020
I'll be staying in Japan until then.

54
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:11,220
Good morning.

55
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:13,300
Good morning, Chief.

56
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,060
Nakagawa

57
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:18,620
Yes, what is it, Chief?

58
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:22,580
Mr. Nakagawa, you don't look well at all.

59
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:26,380
I bet Ryotsu wrecked yesterday's wedding.

60
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,492
No, no,

61
00:05:27,542 --> 00:05:33,020
the wedding went wonderfully. Senpai managed everything,
and it was a huge success.

62
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:36,040
I can't believe that Ryotsu.

63
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:41,040
Well, everyone did get completely smashed in the end,
so it was a bit rough.

64
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:43,360
I thought as much.

65
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,220
Good morning, everyone.

66
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:47,220
Good morning, Master Ryo.

67
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,580
Speak of the devil.

68
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:52,860
Wow, yesterday's wedding was a blast,
wasn't it?

69
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,360
Y-yes, senpai.

70
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:59,200
Don't call me senpai. That's too formal.

71
00:05:59,200 --> 00:06:04,280
That's right, Master Ryo. You're officially
related to Mr. Nakagawa now, aren't you?

72
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:14,000
Kinjiro's new bride is the daughter of the younger brother of the second wife of the eldest
son of the daughter of the ex-wife of the son of Nakagawa's grandma's younger sister, right?

73
00:06:14,020 --> 00:06:14,380
Uh-huh.

74
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:20,900
That makes Nakagawa and me relatives,
meaning family.

75
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:24,060
Well, if it's that distant,
I don't think you'd call them family.

76
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,820
No, there's no such thing as distant family.

77
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:32,640
So, Nakagawa,
from today on I'm calling you Kei-chan.

78
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:36,300
Kei-chan, you'll call me
"big brother" from now on too.

79
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,620
Y-yes...

80
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:38,276
Ryotsu,

81
00:06:38,326 --> 00:06:42,280
Nakagawa isn't your sibling, so
"big brother" is weird, isn't it?

82
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:46,100
Chief, please don't go telling
outsiders anything about family matters.

83
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:50,720
Then how about this: you call me
"Relative-san."

84
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,000
"Relative-san"...?

85
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:53,781
Kei-chan,

86
00:06:53,831 --> 00:06:58,680
Since we're family now, if you have any worries or troubles,
come talk to me about anything.

87
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:05,060
It's like Nakagawa has a freeloader living under his roof,
isn't it.

88
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:06,140
Yes.

89
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:07,860
That's...

90
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:10,320
It's a book about the Nakagawa Group.

91
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:11,820
What's the matter?

92
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:15,700
You'll need to learn a lot about
the Nakagawa Group from now on.

93
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,000
As family.

94
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,980
So, as family, I've put together a
table of the group's main companies.

95
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:23,480
Even that much?

96
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,980
You really are meticulous when
it comes to this sort of thing.

97
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:28,140
Because she's the lady of the house,
after all.

98
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,378
Railways, pharmaceuticals, automobiles,

99
00:07:30,428 --> 00:07:32,820
telecommunications and so
on are growing steadily, but

100
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,143
the problem is real estate,

101
00:07:34,193 --> 00:07:36,940
securities and other affiliated subsidiaries:
163 companies.

102
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:38,080
That's the trouble.

103
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:40,440
Operating profit is lower than last year.

104
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,700
Even things I don't know myself,

105
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,260
I can't just leave this alone as family.

106
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,400
No, you can leave it alone, really.

107
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,380
I'll storm into the company and
give them a good kick in the pants.

108
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:54,740
I've rescued several small
companies in the old town before.

109
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:55,600
Leave it to me.

110
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:58,220
But if you just show up at
the company out of nowhere,

111
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,480
don't worry.

112
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,400
That's why I had business cards made.

113
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,220
Relative.

114
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:05,260
With these,
they'll know right away we're family, right?

115
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:06,920
Even something like this...

116
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:08,060
Ryo-sama, you're amazing.

117
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:08,880
Right?

118
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:12,260
Nakagawa, a moment.

119
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,680
If you provoke him carelessly,
he could bring the whole company down.

120
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:19,380
You'd better do as he says on this one.

121
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:22,160
But you need to fool him smoothly,

122
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:24,420
and give him some harmless work.

123
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:25,320
I see.

124
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:27,300
Yes, that would certainly be safer.

125
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,260
I've found a job you'd like him to do.

126
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,880
So which company is it?

127
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,800
It's the company on the Katsudoki side.

128
00:08:33,800 --> 00:08:34,740
Katsudoki.

129
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:36,860
Good, I'm great with the old downtown areas.

130
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:39,060
Nakagawa, let's do our best!

131
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,240
As family, of course.

132
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,840
Y-yes.

133
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,220
You're Kankichi Ryotsu, correct?

134
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:50,200
I've heard all about you
from young master Kei-chan.

135
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,960
I'm Kurokawa, the president.

136
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,120
Pleased to meet you.

137
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,500
The pleasure is mine.

138
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:55,960
So, what will my job be?

139
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,520
Some job that only I can do,
or something like that?

140
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:01,680
Yes, you'll be a Super Guard Store Keeper.

141
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,980
Super Guard Store Keeper?

142
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:06,720
That sounds like quite a cool job.

143
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:13,180
Damn it, what's this
"Super Guard Store Keeper" nonsense?

144
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:15,740
Put simply,
isn't it just a jack-of-all-trades job?

145
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:19,040
Nakagawa,
tricking your own family like this!

146
00:09:19,040 --> 00:09:22,060
If that's how you want it,
I've got a plan of my own.

147
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:24,700
I want to do sales.

148
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:26,680
Look at this.

149
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,460
Relative-san?

150
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:32,060
W-what, a relative of the Nakagawa Group?

151
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,520
Isn't he just Young
Master Kei-chan's senior?

152
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:37,360
I'm Nakagawa's relative, through marriage.

153
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:40,800
You know, I'm known as dead
weight in the Nakagawa Group.

154
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,840
I want to turn this
money-losing company around.

155
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,300
As family, you see.

156
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:46,540
But from young master Kei-chan,

157
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,240
Shut up! You've only just arrived,
and you're still the president?!

158
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:49,940
Please forgive the violence.

159
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:53,520
I want to make this company the
top firm in the Nakagawa Group.

160
00:09:54,120 --> 00:09:55,420
Don't cooperate with me.

161
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,440
Yes.

162
00:09:57,420 --> 00:10:00,780
Right, then we'll start by
improving the delivery business.

163
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:03,540
First, we'll change the company name.

164
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:08,360
A lame name like
"Nakagawa Transport Delivery Warehouse" won't do in this day and age.

165
00:10:10,220 --> 00:10:13,060
That's right,
let's call it the Unibrow Delivery Service.

166
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:26,080
Alright, Kurokawa,
we're going full steam ahead from now on!

167
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,440
Where to?

168
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,700
Those relatives of the Nakagawa Group.

169
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:36,400
That's right, let me show you the proof.

170
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:37,620
Kurokawa.

171
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:42,760
Here?

172
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,460
See, it's got the name right there.

173
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,280
Fine, fine, I understand.

174
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,420
So, what business does this
relative of yours have, then?

175
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:54,820
The president isn't one to rely
on his relatives' clout, is he?

176
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:58,440
A big corporation can't be
moved by the president alone.

177
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:01,820
Sometimes the whole family opposes it,
and no decision can be made.

178
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:06,680
Keeping that noisy bunch of
relatives in line is my job.

179
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:09,700
In a way, I'm the power behind the scenes.

180
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:13,420
If I say it's black,
every last relative will agree it's black.

181
00:11:13,420 --> 00:11:15,420
In other words, if you make me angry...

182
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,680
If you make me angry...

183
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:18,600
...it's scary.

184
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:22,760
Really?

185
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:24,000
Really.

186
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:30,520
Not to brag, but I'm close enough to President Nakagawa
Ryuichiro that we share meals whenever he visits Japan.

187
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:36,060
No way. I've never had a meal with President Ryuichiro,
not even once.

188
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,600
It's not a lie.

189
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:40,820
When President Ryuichiro came
to Japan half a year ago...

190
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:45,120
we stood side by side under one umbrella and
ate standing-up soba together for fifteen minutes.

191
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,980
Yes, the ever-busy President Ryuichiro is

192
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:51,460
said to eat nothing but
standing soba in Japan.

193
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,600
And he spent fifteen whole minutes with me!

194
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:58,640
That shows how much
President Ryuichiro trusts me.

195
00:11:59,220 --> 00:11:59,755
In other words,

196
00:11:59,805 --> 00:12:04,640
please listen to my words as if
they were the president's own.

197
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:06,860
Understood.

198
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:09,320
Please don't hold back and tell me anything.

199
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,960
Relative Ryo-san.

200
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:12,920
I see.

201
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:16,960
Now, I'd like to consult with you
about the parcel delivery outlets.

202
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:17,660
By all means.

203
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:21,260
That shit-for-brains
might be useful after all.

204
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:36,360
Nakagawa Unyu's delivery
warehouse is making a profit?

205
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:37,460
Yes.

206
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:40,420
Ever since we changed the name
to the Unibrow Delivery Service,

207
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:42,500
we've been rapidly increasing our outlets,

208
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:46,220
and finally reached 300,000 locations,
taking the top spot in the industry.

209
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,380
It's the handiwork of a senior.

210
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:53,880
They've also imported one million tons of grain,
including wheat and corn, from overseas.

211
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:56,940
Yes, it seems they're pouring
all their profits into it.

212
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,120
The L2 phenomenon is also subsiding.

213
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:02,040
Getting involved in grain
from here on is dangerous.

214
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:08,100
I don't think it's right for a president like you,
Kurokawa, to be at the beck and call of a senior.

215
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:11,300
We already have a million tons of wheat.
Aren't the warehouses full?

216
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,320
With all due respect,

217
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:18,460
the one actually running our company now isn't me,
the president, but the chairman.

218
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:19,280
Chairman?

219
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:23,000
Yes, it's Ryotsu,
a relative of the Nakagawa Group.

220
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,600
Wait, the senior is the chairman?

221
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:27,060
Kurokawa-kun.

222
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:28,560
This is the chairman.

223
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:30,840
Kei-chan, you came too.

224
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:33,440
Perfect timing. Take a look at this.

225
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:36,620
A great drought has hit Europe and Russia.

226
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:39,020
Wheat and corn prices have soared.

227
00:13:39,020 --> 00:13:42,060
They've doubled from what we paid.

228
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:49,640
Ahahahahahahaha!

229
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:50,800
Damn it!

230
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:54,600
I was about to deal a crushing
blow to the Nakagawa Group.

231
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,301
Tch, well, never mind.

232
00:13:56,351 --> 00:13:58,760
Good luck can't last forever.

233
00:13:59,280 --> 00:13:59,940
Heh heh.

234
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:00,782
Honestly,

235
00:14:00,832 --> 00:14:04,580
Senpai's dumb luck is truly astonishing.

236
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:08,980
But I thought Kurokawa was so cautious
he'd tap a stone bridge before crossing it,

237
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:12,900
so I made him president of that dead-weight company.
He's changed, though.

238
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:15,200
Senpai is forcing everything through,
that's all.

239
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,900
Isn't it President Kurokawa's fault?

240
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:21,460
Keichi, I'm going to be away
from the company for a while.

241
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:24,080
I'm leaving the rest to you.

242
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:34,960
Right.

243
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:37,020
Time for my energy drink refill.

244
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:43,300
No, I've fallen into my old habit again.

245
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:44,400
This way, then.

246
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:46,720
Hey.

247
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:51,740
Damn it.

248
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:54,580
What, you're quite the drama queen,
aren't you?

249
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:58,120
Nakagawa-kun has been
working here since today.

250
00:14:58,120 --> 00:14:58,800
Y-yes.

251
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:03,560
Nakagawa, is it?
I feel like I've met you somewhere before.

252
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,160
W-we've just met for the first time.

253
00:15:05,160 --> 00:15:08,640
I see, you must resemble someone.
Think, think!

254
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:11,060
That's it.

255
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:13,160
Wrong... or rather, busted

256
00:15:13,660 --> 00:15:15,000
That mustache looks cool.

257
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:16,160
I'll grow one myself.

258
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:16,860
Mustache?

259
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:19,520
Kurokawa,
go buy me one at Kappabashi tomorrow.

260
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,020
Very well.

261
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:23,760
That sound...

262
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:26,440
It's drink time!

263
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:52,000
Trying to copy me, are you?

264
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:55,860
What's with that face?
Got a problem with it?

265
00:15:55,860 --> 00:16:01,680
Not at all. I just thought that someone who
has become chairman is really something else.

266
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,940
I see. You're a pretty good guy, aren't you.

267
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:08,040
It'd be a waste to keep
it as a warehouse version.

268
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:12,740
I like you! Nakagawa, be my driver!

269
00:16:13,380 --> 00:16:15,460
Y-yes...

270
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:18,100
This is convenient.

271
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,240
Chairman Ohara.

272
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:23,020
What is it?

273
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:25,653
About the 30 billion yen you made from wheat,
Chairman,

274
00:16:25,703 --> 00:16:28,040
how about investing it in stocks?

275
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:31,636
Good idea.
I'm on a winning streak right now.

276
00:16:31,686 --> 00:16:33,320
Is there any good stock?

277
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:35,720
How about Katamuki Seiyaku?

278
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:41,180
It's at that level right now, but I have
information that it's definitely going to go up.

279
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:45,040
Katamuki Pharmaceutical is a
company on the verge of bankruptcy.

280
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:47,380
What on earth is Kurokawa thinking?

281
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:51,220
Good, use the 30 billion to
buy up all of those shares.

282
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:54,900
Whoa, hey, what do you think you're doing?

283
00:16:55,880 --> 00:17:00,640
Sorry, but I don't think putting
all 30 billion into it is wise.

284
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:04,100
Well, are you saying you'll
argue with the chairman?

285
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:05,360
Ha

286
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:10,800
Understood, Chairman. I'll contact the brokerage
right away and have them buy up the shares.

287
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:12,220
Leave it to you.

288
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:15,500
This time, the company is finished for sure.

289
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:20,680
What? Katamuki Pharmaceutical has
developed a miracle cure for athlete's foot.

290
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:25,540
I can't stop laughing!

291
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:30,900
All of this is thanks to Kurokawa's advice.

292
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:35,160
Looks like Kurokawa's expectations
completely fell through.

293
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,540
That's quite something, isn't it.

294
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,680
Ryotsu made over 100 billion yen in stocks?

295
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:46,320
It was one ridiculous streak
of dumb luck after another,

296
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:48,080
and in just a month and a half,

297
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:50,580
he turned it into the most profitable
company in the Nakagawa Group.

298
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:51,940
That's how much it grew.

299
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:54,540
Wow! Ryo-sama, that's amazing!

300
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:57,240
No, this is Ryotsu's usual pattern.

301
00:17:57,240 --> 00:18:01,180
At first, everything goes smoothly,

302
00:18:01,180 --> 00:18:04,380
but at the very end, there's always a twist.

303
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,880
Nakagawa, you'd better make a move quickly.

304
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:10,660
Yes, I thought so too,
but it's already too late.

305
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:14,140
Senpai already took the
100 billion yen he made

306
00:18:14,140 --> 00:18:16,700
and left for America for a business deal.

307
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:21,060
He's signing contracts one after another, all
by himself, without going through an interpreter.

308
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:23,980
He's importing absolutely
everything from America.

309
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:26,400
That guy can't even speak English, can he?

310
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:30,020
It seems he's making deals by saying nothing but
"yes" and "no."

311
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:31,670
With Ryo-sama's pushiness,

312
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:34,040
he could probably close
a deal even with aliens.

313
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:36,240
It's not Nami's pushiness, though.

314
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:46,960
Because of that, every company warehouse is full, so they're storing the overflow in the next shipment's processing area.
Looks like the termites have finally started gnawing on the pillars.

315
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:59,160
Just drive around for about an hour. Yes, well,
Ryotsu isn't supposed to be back from America until tomorrow.

316
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:01,880
What on earth are you going to Narita for?

317
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:05,980
That's...

318
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:08,740
Isn't that the president of Ibishi Trading?

319
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:11,340
Kurokawa, you've finally shown your tail!

320
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,600
Chairman Ohara.

321
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,480
Weren't you supposed to return tomorrow?

322
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:25,540
I finished my work early.

323
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:28,520
More importantly, what are you doing here?

324
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,780
Nothing in particular.

325
00:19:29,780 --> 00:19:31,180
That's a camera, isn't it?

326
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:35,680
Yes, I'm into photography.
Damn, I just wasted a great chance.

327
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:39,533
That's right! Then take a picture of me.

328
00:19:39,583 --> 00:19:43,000
I was just wanting a portrait
to hang in the chairman's office.

329
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:46,271
Yes, Chairman. That's convenient.

330
00:19:46,321 --> 00:19:49,420
Lighting is everything.
This way, please. Come on, right this way.

331
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,920
Yes, Chairman. You look great.

332
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,500
Chairman, a little more to the right.

333
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:56,140
Like this?

334
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:57,680
Yes, that's good.

335
00:19:58,460 --> 00:20:00,480
Perfect, Chairman.

336
00:20:01,880 --> 00:20:03,500
So it's a sure thing, then?

337
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:06,960
After the 100,000 American cars,

338
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:08,820
nata de coco and kombucha next?

339
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:10,140
Senpai,

340
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:13,020
you should stop with the
risky investments already.

341
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:14,320
What are you talking about?

342
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:16,520
The world revolves around me!

343
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:17,640
But...

344
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:20,960
Relax, I'll make the Nakagawa
Group twice its current size.

345
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:22,540
I'll lend you a hand.

346
00:20:22,540 --> 00:20:23,840
As family, of course.

347
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:28,220
Bringing a crushing blow to
the Nakagawa Group as a gift,

348
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:29,880
the plan I had to move over to Ibishi,

349
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,720
but now that it's come to this...

350
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:40,520
C-Chairman! Isn't delivering
dangerous goods risky after all?

351
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:43,980
Idiot! The advantage is precisely
that no one else is doing it!

352
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:47,680
Also, being open 365 days a year,
24 hours a day...

353
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:52,980
What are you talking about! That's why we installed full automation equipment,
isn't it?

354
00:20:53,030 --> 00:20:55,500
The whole point of machines is
that they can work without rest!

355
00:20:55,500 --> 00:20:58,352
But if there's no time for maintenance,

356
00:20:58,402 --> 00:21:01,740
if the machines malfunction,
it'll be a disaster...

357
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,660
Don't worry. I'll keep a proper eye on...

358
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,720
Whoa! H-he brought a bonfire!

359
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,880
Oh no! If that's a fire,
we're in big trouble!

360
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:10,320
Ouch, hot!

361
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:21,980
Put out the fire quickly!

362
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:24,260
It's too late, Chairman! Let's run!

363
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:27,780
The 100 billion yen I made

364
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:34,560
from wheat, corn, candy,
semiconductors, nata de coco, and kombucha

365
00:21:42,140 --> 00:21:43,860
Looks like he went big again.

366
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,980
What will happen to Ryo-sama?

367
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:48,140
With damage this big,

368
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:51,180
he's surely going to be
expelled from the Nakagawa Group.

369
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,600
It's because of that reckless plan.

370
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:55,720
No way!

371
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,000
Chairman, quiet!

372
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,380
I'll state the conclusion first.

373
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:03,060
Ryotsu will be stepping down as chairman,

374
00:22:03,800 --> 00:22:06,920
but we won't hold him
responsible for this matter at all.

375
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:11,780
But who is responsible for leaving
a stain on the Nakagawa Group's name?

376
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:16,140
Never mind that. Thanks to Ryotsu-kun,
we've found out who the traitor is.

377
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:16,780
What did you say?!

378
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:17,980
Who is it?

379
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:19,860
The traitor is

380
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:21,900
this man!

381
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:22,420
What?!

382
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:25,380
Chief, please stop this bad joke!

383
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:27,380
What makes you say something like that...?

384
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:29,900
Hmph, here's the proof!

385
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:33,300
That?

386
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:35,982
Kurokawa not only defected
to the Ibishi Group,

387
00:22:36,032 --> 00:22:38,160
he even masterminded this
latest major accident!

388
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:39,420
What, s-stop!

389
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:42,560
Are you still going to
play innocent after this?!

390
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:47,920
Driver!

391
00:22:48,260 --> 00:22:49,760
Damn it... dammit...

392
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:57,100
On suspicion of aggravated breach
of trust against the parent company,

393
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:58,620
an arrest warrant has been issued.

394
00:22:58,620 --> 00:23:00,120
You're coming with us.

395
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,960
And that settles the matter.

396
00:23:07,820 --> 00:23:09,440
Thanks, Ryu-chan. You saved me.

397
00:23:09,860 --> 00:23:10,700
Ryu-chan.

398
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:12,340
Let's keep working together.

399
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,400
As family.

400
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:16,540
If we're family,
I never heard anything about this.

401
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:18,240
So we're not family?

402
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,160
What?

403
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:22,018
No my younger brother's wife is -

404
00:23:22,068 --> 00:23:25,340
Nakagawa's grandma's younger
sister's son's ex-wife...

405
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:26,420
Time's up.

406
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:27,280
Ah...

407
00:23:30,760 --> 00:23:33,040
Well then, see you again in ten years!

408
00:23:34,100 --> 00:23:35,220
Farewell!

409
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:38,720
Dad! Take care!

410
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:40,760
Kei-chan.

411
00:23:41,680 --> 00:23:44,660
As family, could you introduce
me to somewhere else sometime?

412
00:23:45,120 --> 00:23:48,440
Since Dad doesn't accept me as family,
that's a bit...

413
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:49,900
Come on.

414
00:23:50,350 --> 00:23:51,800
And that way of addressing me, too...

415
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:53,760
No, hey, wait!

416
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:55,780
Don't run away, everyone!

417
00:23:55,780 --> 00:23:57,260
We're relatives, aren't we?

418
00:23:57,260 --> 00:23:58,540
That's cold!

419
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,040
As family...

420
00:24:15,460 --> 00:24:17,800
With surprise and commotion,

421
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:21,540
look, look, please, please,

422
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:25,380
whoa, unpredictable!

423
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:29,460
decided in a flash, and inspiration strikes,

424
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:30,940
whoa, bouncing along,

425
00:24:30,940 --> 00:24:32,400
debe debe, gathering it all together,

426
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:35,360
into action, and off we fly,

427
00:24:36,020 --> 00:24:40,060
above all, the power is incredible!

428
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:45,980
everybody, gather, if you come here,

429
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:52,400
the dreamlike, ultimate energy.

430
00:24:53,420 --> 00:24:56,440
Gazing at tomorrow, your hat

431
00:24:56,440 --> 00:24:59,700
Painting the whole globe,
standing on the ground

432
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:03,480
The Kameari star spun
around and drew a circle

433
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:07,140
This should be fine, right?

434
00:25:07,140 --> 00:25:08,600
Of course it's not fine!

435
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:23,300
It's you again, you crazy professor!

436
00:25:23,300 --> 00:25:24,200
What did you just say?

437
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:26,520
The video I need for the
conference the day after tomorrow

438
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:29,060
You mistakenly sent it
to one of your daughters?!

439
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:30,340
Anyway, whatever...

440
00:25:30,340 --> 00:25:33,340
Why are your daughters
even in a place like that?

441
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:36,380
Next time: Around the world in 48 hours

442
00:25:36,380 --> 00:25:37,360
See you then.

